The TypeScript adaptation keeps the float arithmetic of the plain C formula
(each product, difference and store rounded to float, no fused multiply-add),
as the Linux x86-64 reference evaluates it. It refuses timeline enable, runtime
commands, option expressions, non-stereo or masked layouts that native would
convert implicitly, and non-finite input samples, instead of approximating them.
It adds no FFmpeg runtime code. The original source and full notices remain in
the pinned upstream submodule.
